1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,921
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:43,961
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,880
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,012
[Ahin] There's a ghost
in the abandoned house.

7
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:56,765
I'm sure it's some kind of vengeful ghost.

8
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:59,393
It's asking us to catch the killer.

9
00:00:59,476 --> 00:01:00,852
-Let's go check it out.
-What?

10
00:01:00,936 --> 00:01:02,437
PREVIOUSLY

11
00:01:02,521 --> 00:01:04,523
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

12
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:05,899
[Isoo exhales]

13
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:07,985
[Hyera] You check upstairs.

14
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,117
[blunt thuds]

15
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:17,494
Nutjob!

16
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:19,538
-Yes, ma'am!
-[Hyera grunts]

17
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,123
[Isoo] What's going on?

18
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:23,083
-Hey, what happened?
-I don't know.

19
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:25,335
I got attacked out of nowhere.

20
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,878
[♪ upbeat suspenseful music playing]

21
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:32,384
-One... Two, three!
-Two, three!

22
00:01:32,968 --> 00:01:33,969
[Hyera grunts]

23
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:37,431
[glass shattering]

24
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:40,517
[explosion]

25
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,272
I seriously almost died.

26
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,399
There really is something here.

27
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:49,359
I have great instincts, huh?

28
00:01:49,443 --> 00:01:52,362
Let's open it up.
There's definitely something in there.

29
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,740
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

30
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,296
You were there.

31
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,673
I started the fire.

32
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:14,217
They might've found something
while putting out the fire.

33
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,261
Hyeonsu disappeared.

34
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,597
Hyeonsu's last location was that house.

35
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,349
[Changun] You uncovered five bodies?

36
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:22,643
Yes, they're performing the autopsy now.

37
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:24,978
[Dr. Yoon] We performed the autopsy
on the most recent victim first.

38
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:27,397
The most recently deceased victim

39
00:02:27,481 --> 00:02:29,024
had these glasses in their pants.

40
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,026
These belong to Park Hyeonsu.

41
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:32,486
Three months ago, at Yuseon-dong...

42
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,570
-[muffled screaming]
-[flesh squelching]

43
00:02:33,654 --> 00:02:35,322
[Byungsik] ...Kim Minseo was murdered.

44
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,741
[Kim Suwon] Park Hyeonsu's fingerprints
were on a knife at the scene.

45
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:41,161
That knife was the knife
missing from Park Hyeonsu's house.

46
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:42,245
MURDER SUSPECT

47
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:43,455
[Junyoung] Wait, so,

48
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:46,667
the murder suspect you were after
three months ago was murdered

49
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:49,670
and his body was found
at the abandoned house?

50
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:52,464
What if Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one
who killed Kim Minseo?

51
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:53,965
It's the perfect crime.

52
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:55,634
The target.

53
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,761
A victim to frame as the suspect.

54
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:00,055
If they kill the target and the suspect,

55
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:01,807
then make him go missing,

56
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,309
the case cannot be solved.

57
00:03:05,769 --> 00:03:07,646
[Hyera] Five perfect crimes.

58
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:10,107
You need at least two people
to make this possible.

59
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:12,275
-They're methodical and cold.
-[Hyeonsu grunting]

60
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:14,277
[Kyungjin] So they're
professional killers?

61
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:16,279
If they came to the house...

62
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:18,448
It means they killed someone else.

63
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:20,409
They were there to bury the body.

64
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,332
[Jaechun] It's blood. [exclaims]

65
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:28,583
KILLER 1
JANG JAECHUN

66
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:29,793
It leaked.

67
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:30,877
KILLER 2
JO BEOMKI

68
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:32,170
What do we do?

69
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:34,381
Taegwang.

70
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:45,976
THE KILLER OF KILLERS
YU TAEGWANG

71
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,646
[♪ tense music playing]

72
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:52,023
But don't courier deliveries come quickly

73
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:54,317
and drop it off at the door?

74
00:03:54,401 --> 00:03:56,695
They're a bit different
from parcel deliveries.

75
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:58,071
They usually hand it to you.

76
00:03:58,155 --> 00:03:59,197
Uh-huh.

77
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:03,869
Then the victim must have known
a courier was coming.

78
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:06,997
Yes, they usually contact ahead.

79
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,499
But this wasn't a real courier.

80
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:11,626
So someone must've helped them.

81
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,712
To make her open the door.

82
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:16,548
It must be the one she lives with.

83
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,425
Her husband.

84
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,469
Who is her husband?

85
00:04:22,179 --> 00:04:24,848
Nam Jaeguk.
He's the CEO of a furniture company.

86
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:29,853
IDENTITY RECORD
NAM JAEGUK

87
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,063
Detective Choi, you look into Nam Jaeguk.

88
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,775
And check
if Kim Minseo had life insurance.

89
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,777
-Yes, ma'am.
-Detective Park.

90
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,320
You look into the stalking case.

91
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:39,529
Understood.

92
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,031
We'll meet Nam Jaeguk tomorrow.

93
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:42,616
Okay.

94
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,418
[Hyera] We're with the police.

95
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:56,671
Is Mr. Nam Jaeguk here?

96
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:59,257
Yes, what is this about?

97
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:02,719
Well, his wife was brutally murdered.

98
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:04,971
Do you happen to know anything?

99
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:07,557
Like the CEO's secret, for example?

100
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,936
[chuckles softly] You think I'd know that?

101
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:12,312
Please take us to see him.

102
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,110
EPISODE 4

103
00:05:19,194 --> 00:05:20,695
Don't go probing just anyone.

104
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:22,572
This is an investigation technique.

105
00:05:22,656 --> 00:05:24,866
Didn't you know? Huh?

106
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:25,951
[mutters] Honestly.

107
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:31,122
[♪ tense music playing]

108
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:33,333
KIM MINSEO'S HUSBAND
NAM JAEGUK

109
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,543
What...

110
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:37,295
is this about?

111
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:41,341
We're here about your wife's case.

112
00:05:42,801 --> 00:05:44,636
You're not the detective in charge.

113
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:47,055
We're reinvestigating
the case from scratch.

114
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,601
Reinvestigating?

115
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,105
Park Hyeonsu's the culprit.

116
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:57,607
Isn't he?

117
00:05:57,691 --> 00:06:00,902
Mmm. Someone else might be the culprit.

118
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:03,780
-Couldn't they?
-[scoffs]

119
00:06:04,239 --> 00:06:07,284
[Hyera] We heard your wife
was being stalked.

120
00:06:08,285 --> 00:06:09,911
Was the stalker Park Hyeonsu?

121
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:11,246
Yes. [sighs]

122
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,665
I've already told the police all this.

123
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,667
Don't you share information?

124
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:16,793
[scoffs]

125
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,837
Please tell us again.

126
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,840
Did you hear anything about Park Hyeonsu?

127
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:22,924
[Jaeguk inhales deeply]

128
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:25,260
They dated briefly in college,

129
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:28,555
then ran into each other
by chance recently.

130
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:31,725
After that, he followed her around,
trying to get back together.

131
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,352
That's what she said.

132
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:37,689
You mean your wife,
Ms. Kim Minseo, said that herself?

133
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:40,400
Yes, she did.
Why are you bringing this up again now?

134
00:06:41,318 --> 00:06:42,903
Park Hyeonsu

135
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:44,696
has been found.

136
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:50,702
How did you find him?

137
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:55,999
Mmm, I can't tell you.
That's classified information.

138
00:06:58,001 --> 00:07:00,128
We came to update you on your wife's case.

139
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:02,213
We'll be in touch.

140
00:07:11,556 --> 00:07:13,725
Her husband definitely ordered the murder.

141
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:16,853
How do you know?

142
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:19,481
"I am guilty"
was written all over his face.

143
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,900
That was pretty much a confession.

144
00:07:22,901 --> 00:07:24,527
There's something else.

145
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:27,989
-What?
-When we said Park Hyeonsu had been found,

146
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:30,492
he didn't ask if we'd caught him.

147
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:33,203
How did you find him?

148
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:35,538
Right, that's true.

149
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:38,708
His first concern should've been
whether we'd caught the guy.

150
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:42,003
-It's because he knows the guy's dead.
-[softly] Hmm.

151
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:45,382
Hey, take care.

152
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,345
[♪ ominous music playing]

153
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:59,145
[breathing raggedly]

154
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,024
Where's my damn phone?

155
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:17,872
[man] After today, you mustn't
call me, no matter what happens.

156
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:19,582
[♪ foreboding music playing]

157
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,889
[exhales deeply]

158
00:08:34,973 --> 00:08:37,475
During the month
before Ms. Kim Minseo died,

159
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:39,477
she filed three stalking reports.

160
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:42,230
STALKING REPORT

161
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,859
Did you question the suspect?

162
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,444
No, we weren't able to.

163
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,778
She didn't know who it was.

164
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:52,699
She just reported that someone had been
following her near her house.

165
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:56,369
Ah, for the last report,

166
00:08:56,453 --> 00:08:59,789
she deliberately caused a fender bender
because someone was following her.

167
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:01,332
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

168
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:08,882
10 DAYS BEFORE KIM MINSEO'S DEATH

169
00:09:13,428 --> 00:09:15,180
Hello, we're responding to a report.

170
00:09:15,263 --> 00:09:20,060
Yes, I did cause the accident,
but I think that man in the car behind me

171
00:09:20,143 --> 00:09:22,520
has been stalking me for a few days now.

172
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:24,022
That's why I did it.

173
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:25,482
What are you talking about?

174
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:26,566
Hey, lady.

175
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:28,735
Why would I follow you around?

176
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,445
You have. You've been following me.

177
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:32,697
Lady, are you crazy? Delusional much?

178
00:09:32,781 --> 00:09:33,782
[officer] But...

179
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:35,408
Both of you, please calm down.

180
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:37,660
Why would I follow you?
Don't be ridiculous.

181
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:39,746
IDENTITY RECORD
LEE KYUNGSU

182
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:45,251
[line connects, ringing]

183
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,715
Kyungjin, get a location on this number.

184
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:52,509
010-0675-0040.

185
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:55,887
PARK HYEONSU'S HOUSE

186
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,222
Did you find anything?

187
00:09:57,305 --> 00:10:00,016
Just some fingerprints
and a few strands of hair.

188
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:03,103
-Please run them as quickly as possible.
-Got it.

189
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,568
Hey.

190
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:16,783
KIM MINSEO 4:00 P.M.

191
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,744
They met three months before the incident.

192
00:10:19,828 --> 00:10:20,912
Why did they meet?

193
00:10:21,579 --> 00:10:22,831
They had no contact before.

194
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:25,625
Hmm...

195
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:28,002
[♪ gripping music playing]

196
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:51,651
-Found it.
-[mouse clicking]

197
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:58,825
[Minseo] This is Minseo.
It's been a while.

198
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,077
I hope you've been well.

199
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,788
I heard you became a lawyer.

200
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,624
I want to ask your advice on something.

201
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:09,544
Could we possibly meet?

202
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:11,796
I need your help.

203
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,092
Kim Minseo was the one
who asked to meet first.

204
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,011
Why?

205
00:11:18,595 --> 00:11:19,596
Because of this?

206
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:26,644
[♪ upbeat jaunty music playing]

207
00:11:26,728 --> 00:11:27,729
[Isoo] Look familiar?

208
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,732
-[scoffs]
-[chuckles softly]

209
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:33,401
I don't go around
probing people for no reason.

210
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:36,070
It's my detective's instinct.

211
00:11:36,154 --> 00:11:37,322
[in English] Understand?

212
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:41,034
Mmm-hmm. Mmm.

213
00:11:43,995 --> 00:11:46,122
[camera beeping, shutter clicking]

214
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:51,628
[gasps softly]

215
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,255
[in Korean] Who are you?

216
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:56,799
Police.

217
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:00,470
I haven't done anything wrong.

218
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:03,181
You're parked illegally, for one.

219
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,557
Am I getting a ticket?

220
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:07,435
Did you follow this person?

221
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:09,604
[sighs]

222
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,148
Is that your answer?

223
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:13,983
Yes, I followed her.

224
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,278
What about this man?

225
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,989
I took pictures of them meeting.

226
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:22,575
Who hired you?

227
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:26,704
[exclaims] How would I know that?
It's just a part-time gig I do sometimes.

228
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:30,250
Besides, I don't work with them anymore.

229
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,085
-Why not?
-[sighs softly]

230
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:36,506
That woman died after I took those photos.

231
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,216
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

232
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:39,425
It kept bothering me.

233
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,594
It felt weird from the start.

234
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:44,097
I was told to get proof
they were having an affair,

235
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,599
but all they did
was drink coffee and talk.

236
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:49,018
They didn't even seem close.

237
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:54,023
[sighs softly]
Where was that place you worked?

238
00:12:55,984 --> 00:12:57,652
I'll start the briefing.

239
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:01,572
Nam Jaeguk married Kim Minseo in 2021.

240
00:13:01,656 --> 00:13:04,951
The furniture company he runs
was originally his father-in-law's.

241
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,161
And Kim Minseo's life insurance payout

242
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:09,122
is one billion won.

243
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,040
He became a CEO thanks to his in-laws.

244
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:14,085
[exhales deeply]
Then killed her for the insurance payout?

245
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,295
Mm-mm. Mm-mm.

246
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:17,213
He's worse than that.

247
00:13:20,383 --> 00:13:22,468
-[scoffs]
-[Isoo] He even cheated on her.

248
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:25,054
With his secretary.

249
00:13:25,138 --> 00:13:27,140
This is straight out of a soap opera.

250
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:30,685
Kim Minseo knew about the affair
and wanted a divorce,

251
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:33,062
which is why she met Park Hyeonsu.

252
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:36,941
[bangs table]
Rather than get fired and end up divorced,

253
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:38,776
Nam Jaeguk chose to kill his wife.

254
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:42,739
It's clear that Nam Jaeguk was the one
who hired someone to kill Kim Minseo.

255
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:46,576
The question is, who did he hire?

256
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:48,661
There's a PI involved.

257
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:52,081
A top PI, apparently.

258
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:55,752
What's this?

259
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:56,878
A top PI?

260
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,298
The stalker Kim Minseo reported
used to work here.

261
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,924
All he did was tail her.

262
00:14:02,008 --> 00:14:03,968
He took photos of her
meeting Park Hyeonsu.

263
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,305
He doesn't look like a top PI.

264
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:08,806
He looks kind of dopey.

265
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,725
His name is Myeong Seokho.

266
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:12,393
Two fraud convictions.

267
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:15,229
Let's go catch that dopey PI!

268
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:17,065
Oh. Don't you dare.

269
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:18,191
Why not?

270
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:20,193
He can just deny it.

271
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:22,653
What if he says
they were just hired to tail her?

272
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,323
[Byungsik] She's right.

273
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:26,824
We don't have any evidence.

274
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,787
Myeong Seokho may have planned it,
but someone else did the work.

275
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,999
If we want to catch them...

276
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:39,879
We should just hire them ourselves.

277
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,422
Let's hire them to kill someone.

278
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:43,091
[Junyoung] Right.

279
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:45,593
We'll plant a bug,
then wait until the hitmen call.

280
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,428
If we trace it, we'll get their location.

281
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:48,638
[scoffs softly]

282
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:50,640
Is this how you normally investigate?

283
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,767
Hey, it's a trade secret.

284
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:56,687
[chuckles softly] I know it seems
a little weird, but it does work.

285
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:58,272
You know our track record.

286
00:14:58,356 --> 00:15:00,274
[♪ quirky music playing]

287
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:03,528
[sighs softly]

288
00:15:05,113 --> 00:15:07,824
Come on, we have no evidence.
What if they run?

289
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,367
[clock ticking rapidly]

290
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:13,788
[sighs]

291
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:15,790
Fine. Let's try it.

292
00:15:17,125 --> 00:15:18,126
[Junyoung] Okay.

293
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,337
Then, shall I pose as the client?

294
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,381
Mm-mm. You did it last season.

295
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:26,551
We need someone who looks like
they've got some kind of a past.

296
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:28,261
[sighs]

297
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,680
Did any theater as a kid?

298
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:32,056
No.

299
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:33,808
No.

300
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:37,228
My hands start shaking
when I'm dealt a decent hand in poker.

301
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,396
[chuckles softly]

302
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,482
[breathes sharply]

303
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:43,734
It should be someone older.

304
00:15:43,818 --> 00:15:46,362
And look like they'd want someone dead.

305
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:49,782
Someone with that
cold-blooded mobster vibe.

306
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,742
Does no one fit that bill?

307
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:55,204
What are you all doing? Where's my update?

308
00:15:58,124 --> 00:15:59,208
[chuckles softly]

309
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,336
Oh...

310
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,297
He looks like he could act.

311
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,388
[cell phone vibrating]

312
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,184
[chuckles softly]

313
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:20,188
-Yes, Detective Jin.
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi.

314
00:16:20,271 --> 00:16:22,315
-I need to borrow your car.
-My car?

315
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:24,859
Right now. There's no time.
Send it to the station.

316
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,360
What are you...

317
00:16:26,444 --> 00:16:27,653
We've got hitmen to catch.

318
00:16:27,737 --> 00:16:29,322
There's a suit in the car, right?

319
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:31,574
I need a suit and a watch. Right now.

320
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,326
[♪ quirky dramatic music playing]

321
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:35,077
[exhales]

322
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:37,830
[inhales deeply]

323
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:39,207
Stop the car.

324
00:16:45,922 --> 00:16:48,382
Another car will be here shortly.

325
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:50,259
I'm sorry, sir.

326
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:51,636
Not at all.

327
00:16:51,719 --> 00:16:53,763
I'm used to this.

328
00:16:57,475 --> 00:16:59,143
[♪ intriguing music playing]

329
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,455
[Taegyun] Who is that?

330
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,332
Did we arrest a mob boss?

331
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:22,917
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

332
00:17:23,501 --> 00:17:24,543
Isn't that Chief Park?

333
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:26,754
Gosh...

334
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:30,216
What are they doing?

335
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:32,176
-[car door closes]
-I have no idea, sir.

336
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:46,148
There's something wrong
with our whole station.

337
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,526
[sighs in exasperation] Good grief.

338
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:01,080
MYEONG SEOKHO

339
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,790
[in-game thudding, chiming]

340
00:18:02,873 --> 00:18:03,958
-[in-game Korean chatter]
-[mouse clicks]

341
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,084
[in-game fanfare]

342
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:10,047
It's really taking a nosedive.

343
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:17,597
[♪ tense music playing]

344
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,390
[door closes, locks]

345
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:30,776
Who are you?

346
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:33,738
[Changun grunts]

347
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:36,365
[metal cupboard clangs]

348
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:39,368
[metal cupboard clangs]

349
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:41,829
[Changun exhales deeply]

350
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:56,010
Would you like something to drink?

351
00:18:58,054 --> 00:18:59,096
[in a raspy voice, in English] Cold brew.

352
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:01,015
Decaf.

353
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,309
Light vanilla.

354
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:05,269
Toffee nut latte.

355
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:13,444
French pistachio.

356
00:19:14,362 --> 00:19:15,780
[in Korean] Frappe, served hot.

357
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:17,615
-Fra...
-Okay. [chuckles nervously]

358
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,159
I'll go get them right away.

359
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:24,622
[door opens]

360
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:26,749
[door closes]

361
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,417
[♪ upbeat music playing]

362
00:19:28,501 --> 00:19:29,502
What in the...

363
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,525
How can I help you?

364
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,153
I've got someone to find.

365
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,322
I heard

366
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,700
you're good at finding people.

367
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:02,618
Oh, yes, well.

368
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:06,288
We are the best in the business.

369
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:15,256
[wicked laughter sounds]

370
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:20,261
What did he do?

371
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:22,763
He stole...

372
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,057
my stash.

373
00:20:25,141 --> 00:20:26,517
What stash?

374
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:32,189
What do you think? Foot cream?

375
00:20:32,690 --> 00:20:33,691
Ah.

376
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,776
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

377
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:36,944
Ah.

378
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:40,114
Then, let's see.

379
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:42,783
We'll sign a contract first. Your name is?
[clears throat]

380
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,286
[laughing menacingly]

381
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:53,169
You want to know...

382
00:20:54,837 --> 00:20:56,130
my name?

383
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:59,008
The hell's wrong with you?

384
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:00,551
Uh... No.

385
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:03,262
[chuckles nervously]

386
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:04,472
No contract necessary.

387
00:21:04,555 --> 00:21:05,556
[exhales nervously]

388
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:08,434
I'll find him no matter what.

389
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,396
[grunts softly]

390
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,939
[♪ quirky dramatic music playing]

391
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,196
Your advance.

392
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:29,455
Whoa!

393
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:32,541
You have three days.

394
00:21:34,084 --> 00:21:37,588
If you haven't found him by then...

395
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:41,634
[thuds]

396
00:21:43,761 --> 00:21:45,846
Cozy office you've got here.

397
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,848
[♪ tense music playing]

398
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:51,769
Half a can of gas
will wipe this place out.

399
00:21:53,187 --> 00:21:55,064
If you're unlucky,

400
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,732
someone might die.

401
00:21:57,316 --> 00:21:58,442
[gulps nervously]

402
00:22:00,611 --> 00:22:02,446
[tremulously] I won't let you down.

403
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:07,451
Let's go.

404
00:22:07,535 --> 00:22:08,536
Yes, boss.

405
00:22:11,831 --> 00:22:12,832
That stings.

406
00:22:16,544 --> 00:22:17,962
[exclaims]

407
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,421
Have a good night, sir.

408
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:23,008
[♪ quirky music playing]

409
00:22:23,092 --> 00:22:24,385
[car alarm chirps]

410
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:30,641
[exhales heavily]
[in normal voice] That was scary.

411
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:33,811
Chief, you were amazing.
That was convincing as hell.

412
00:22:33,894 --> 00:22:34,979
You should be an actor.

413
00:22:35,062 --> 00:22:38,190
I was in the drama club in high school.

414
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:39,441
The Drama Lovers Club.

415
00:22:39,525 --> 00:22:42,444
-[scoffs incredulously]
-I knew it. You were a real scumbag.

416
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:45,531
-That's a compliment, right?
-[both chuckle]

417
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:46,615
Let's go.

418
00:22:46,699 --> 00:22:49,535
Will he buy it, or will he not?

419
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,371
-That is the question.
-[Isoo] Let's go.

420
00:23:16,353 --> 00:23:17,688
Have a good night, boss.

421
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:20,649
-[Junyoung] Thank you, sir.
-Right, keep at it.

422
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:27,781
Hey, any movements?

423
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:28,866
No.

424
00:23:31,285 --> 00:23:33,120
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

425
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:45,716
GANGHA 3-DONG ABANDONED HOUSE FIRE
SCENE OF PAST HOMICIDE

426
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:52,097
STILL DETERMINING THE CAUSE OF THE FIRE

427
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:00,940
[Beomki exclaims]

428
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:04,985
[whimpers]

429
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,029
[♪ ominous music playing]

430
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:13,619
[panting softly]

431
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,873
Fingerprints.

432
00:24:17,957 --> 00:24:19,416
[♪ tense music playing]

433
00:24:21,335 --> 00:24:22,336
[sniffles]

434
00:24:23,671 --> 00:24:25,047
[coughing weakly]

435
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:29,093
[groaning]

436
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:33,806
[♪ foreboding music playing]

437
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:04,712
[breath trembles, mutters]

438
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:17,683
[Kim Suwon] Looks like a burner phone.

439
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:20,769
[Isoo sighs]

440
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,688
[line ringing]

441
00:25:23,564 --> 00:25:24,940
Hey.

442
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,401
We got a new job. Where are you?

443
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:28,569
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

444
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:29,653
The reservoir?

445
00:25:30,487 --> 00:25:32,865
You still haven't taken care of that?

446
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:35,909
Someone set fire to our burial site.

447
00:25:35,993 --> 00:25:37,286
What are you talking about?

448
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,163
There were cops there.

449
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:41,915
Those useless morons.

450
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:45,085
They got scared and couldn't kill them.

451
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:48,255
They just tied them up and bailed.

452
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:49,339
But then,

453
00:25:51,091 --> 00:25:52,760
looks like someone set it on fire.

454
00:25:52,843 --> 00:25:56,346
Wait, so do we make a run for it?

455
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:57,639
Why? They found nothing.

456
00:25:58,390 --> 00:25:59,558
Who's the client?

457
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:00,684
I don't know.

458
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:04,104
Some kind of drug cartel.
He wants me to find someone.

459
00:26:07,066 --> 00:26:08,108
What's his name?

460
00:26:08,192 --> 00:26:09,359
I don't know that either.

461
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:11,028
If I don't find him in three days,

462
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,947
he said he'll set this place on fire.

463
00:26:33,884 --> 00:26:34,968
[scoffs]

464
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:38,013
He's a cop.

465
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,807
[♪ tense music playing]

466
00:26:39,890 --> 00:26:40,891
A cop?

467
00:26:40,974 --> 00:26:42,434
[Junyoung and Kyungjin sigh]

468
00:26:42,518 --> 00:26:43,519
[sighs softly]

469
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:48,148
[sighs]

470
00:26:48,232 --> 00:26:50,776
They must've found the bodies
at our burial site.

471
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:52,778
[splutters] Then what do we do?

472
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:53,904
Don't be scared.

473
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,532
They won't find any evidence.

474
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:59,159
But what about me? What do I do?

475
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:03,622
Burn all the records and go off the grid.

476
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:10,212
[♪ ominous music playing]

477
00:27:11,338 --> 00:27:13,048
[Jaechun and Beomki grunting]

478
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:23,100
[Jaechun panting]

479
00:27:29,690 --> 00:27:30,732
Your phones.

480
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:42,911
[snorts, sniffles]

481
00:27:43,996 --> 00:27:45,080
[Jaechun snorts]

482
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,511
[sighs contentedly]

483
00:28:00,971 --> 00:28:02,306
We're flying out at dawn.

484
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,350
Let's go on vacation.

485
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:07,352
Where do you wanna go?

486
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:10,856
[sniffles]

487
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:14,109
[chuckles softly]

488
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:15,736
[Jaechun and Beomki chuckle]

489
00:28:15,819 --> 00:28:17,654
[♪ tense music playing]

490
00:28:17,738 --> 00:28:20,324
-Hey, get all the files out.
-What?

491
00:28:20,407 --> 00:28:22,659
[yelling] Get all the files out,
right now!

492
00:28:23,327 --> 00:28:24,369
Yes, okay.

493
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:27,289
[mutters frantically]

494
00:28:33,754 --> 00:28:35,088
Freeze.

495
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:38,258
Damn it.

496
00:28:38,342 --> 00:28:39,635
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

497
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,178
[Isoo inhales sharply, exhales]

498
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:44,723
[gate clangs]

499
00:28:54,942 --> 00:28:56,026
[device beeps]

500
00:28:57,361 --> 00:28:58,695
[Seokho, over recorder] The reservoir?

501
00:28:58,779 --> 00:29:01,198
You still haven't taken care of that?

502
00:29:01,281 --> 00:29:02,866
Where's this reservoir?

503
00:29:02,950 --> 00:29:06,662
This is illegal wiretapping!

504
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:10,540
This won't hold up
as evidence in court anyway.

505
00:29:10,624 --> 00:29:11,875
You know that! Right?

506
00:29:11,959 --> 00:29:14,169
You sure we won't find
any evidence over there?

507
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:15,837
I doubt it.

508
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:18,298
[Byungsik sighs]

509
00:29:18,382 --> 00:29:20,008
Right now,

510
00:29:20,717 --> 00:29:22,803
I'm in a real bad mood
because you played me.

511
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:25,722
While we investigate that,

512
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:28,100
the real killers will get away.

513
00:29:29,643 --> 00:29:31,436
Then you'll become the main culprit.

514
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:34,773
No, but... You have no evidence!

515
00:29:37,526 --> 00:29:39,111
Let's see the evidence.

516
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:49,162
-What's your name?
-What?

517
00:29:50,372 --> 00:29:51,498
Your name.

518
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:53,875
Lee Eunjeong.

519
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:55,836
Right, Eunjeong.

520
00:29:55,919 --> 00:29:56,920
Got a boyfriend?

521
00:29:57,921 --> 00:30:00,215
Yes, we're planning to get married.

522
00:30:00,298 --> 00:30:01,299
That's a shame.

523
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:02,384
Congratulations.

524
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:05,262
[inhales sharply]
But will he wait a decade for you?

525
00:30:06,221 --> 00:30:08,265
-What?
-This is a hitman's office.

526
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:10,434
Over five people have been killed already.

527
00:30:10,517 --> 00:30:14,021
Even if you're just a minor accomplice,
you'd get at least 10 years. Right?

528
00:30:14,104 --> 00:30:15,731
-Of course.
-For sure.

529
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:17,232
[Eunjeong] No, I...

530
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:19,484
I don't know anything.

531
00:30:19,568 --> 00:30:21,820
I just took calls and made coffee.

532
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:26,199
I don't know if the judge
will believe that. [clicks tongue]

533
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:28,368
Unless you help us catch the bad guys.

534
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,459
Yeongil Reservoir. It's Yeongil Reservoir.

535
00:30:35,542 --> 00:30:37,210
I heard Mr. Myeong mention it once.

536
00:30:37,294 --> 00:30:38,962
-You idiot.
-Sit down!

537
00:30:39,046 --> 00:30:40,464
[♪ upbeat quirky music playing]

538
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:43,050
They would've bolted by now.

539
00:30:43,759 --> 00:30:45,761
-I'll go check it out.
-Got it.

540
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,179
-[Byungsik] Let's go.
-[team] Yes, sir.

541
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:50,724
You must be in shock. Here, drink this.

542
00:30:52,893 --> 00:30:54,644
Can I go home now?

543
00:30:54,728 --> 00:30:56,605
Of course not. We have to question you.

544
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:57,689
[Eunjeong] What?

545
00:30:57,773 --> 00:31:00,650
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

546
00:31:00,734 --> 00:31:03,236
Gwangjin-gu, Seoul. Lee Eunjeong.

547
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:04,571
You're Korean, right?

548
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:05,906
I don't know.

549
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:08,283
You don't know?

550
00:31:08,992 --> 00:31:10,869
You know the victim, Kim Minseo, right?

551
00:31:10,952 --> 00:31:13,580
I don't know. I really don't know her.

552
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:19,544
You ordered Lee Kyungsu
to tail Ms. Kim Minseo, didn't you?

553
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:29,763
Come on, stop saying you don't know.
You and that dopey PI...

554
00:31:29,846 --> 00:31:31,598
[sobbing] I really don't know.

555
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:35,268
Oh, my God, I want to go home.

556
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:37,938
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

557
00:32:01,962 --> 00:32:03,463
[KCSI officer 1] They torched
the whole thing.

558
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:05,298
[Byungsik sighs heavily]

559
00:32:06,383 --> 00:32:07,843
[KCSI officer 2] There's a suitcase
in the trunk.

560
00:32:32,159 --> 00:32:33,160
It's that car.

561
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:35,120
Please keep tracking them.

562
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:36,204
[officer] Got it.

563
00:32:56,933 --> 00:32:57,934
There's nothing.

564
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:00,854
I need the blue light.

565
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:20,999
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

566
00:33:25,003 --> 00:33:26,338
[line connects, ringing]

567
00:33:28,632 --> 00:33:29,674
Detective Joo.

568
00:33:32,719 --> 00:33:33,845
We got a fingerprint.

569
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:36,765
SCANNING

570
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:41,728
[digital beeps]

571
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:47,651
[Hyera] Jang Jaechun.

572
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:49,569
NAME: JANG JAECHUN

573
00:33:49,653 --> 00:33:51,446
[Junyoung] "Seongju State Prison."

574
00:33:51,529 --> 00:33:52,906
Seongju State Prison?

575
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:58,119
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

576
00:33:59,246 --> 00:34:00,455
2019 SEONGJU STATE PRISON

577
00:34:00,538 --> 00:34:02,958
He was in the same prison
as Myeong Seokho.

578
00:34:04,334 --> 00:34:05,669
Let's look into Jang Jaechun.

579
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:07,420
I'll contact the prison.

580
00:34:07,504 --> 00:34:08,755
I'll look into his family.

581
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:27,649
A phone was found at the reservoir.

582
00:34:27,732 --> 00:34:29,192
We got a fingerprint, too.

583
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:35,156
You have an accomplice. Who is it?

584
00:34:39,327 --> 00:34:40,912
Forensics will recover everything.

585
00:34:43,123 --> 00:34:44,291
[mutters]

586
00:34:44,958 --> 00:34:47,127
You know how a trial works.

587
00:34:47,585 --> 00:34:51,131
Cooperating with the investigation
and showing signs of remorse

588
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:53,800
are important considerations in court.

589
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:56,136
You're out of options now.

590
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:59,264
Wouldn't it be smarter
to try and reduce your sentence?

591
00:35:04,978 --> 00:35:05,979
[Seokho] So...

592
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:09,441
His name's Jo Beomki.

593
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:12,068
He's Jaechun's old classmate.

594
00:35:12,152 --> 00:35:14,571
But all I did was make the introduction.

595
00:35:14,654 --> 00:35:16,323
They asked me for work.

596
00:35:16,406 --> 00:35:19,367
How was I supposed to know
they'd kill someone? I had no idea.

597
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:21,911
Where are they?

598
00:35:23,997 --> 00:35:25,749
I really don't know.

599
00:35:33,506 --> 00:35:34,674
Did you find anything?

600
00:35:35,383 --> 00:35:36,426
No.

601
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:38,762
Nothing much.

602
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:40,722
Myeong Seokho named his accomplice.

603
00:35:44,059 --> 00:35:45,894
-[mouse clicks]
-[keyboard clacking]

604
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:51,358
JO BEOMKI

605
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:53,193
Where are they?

606
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:54,944
He doesn't know.

607
00:35:55,528 --> 00:35:56,696
[sighs softly]

608
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,953
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

609
00:36:11,044 --> 00:36:13,838
Find out where Jang Jaechun
and Jo Beomki are.

610
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:18,343
If making introductions
was really all you did,

611
00:36:19,469 --> 00:36:21,221
you shouldn't go down with them.

612
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:40,949
-[dogs barking distantly]
-[fire crackling]

613
00:36:42,909 --> 00:36:44,202
[cutlery clinking]

614
00:36:45,495 --> 00:36:47,205
[door opens]

615
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,836
[Jaechun exhales deeply]

616
00:36:52,919 --> 00:36:54,087
-[indistinct chatter]
-[grunts]

617
00:36:55,422 --> 00:36:56,548
[Jaechun exclaims]

618
00:36:57,132 --> 00:36:59,467
-[sighs] Granny.
-[Beomki chuckles]

619
00:36:59,551 --> 00:37:01,970
I told you to just go to bed.

620
00:37:02,053 --> 00:37:04,556
[Granny] How can I go to bed
when your friends are here?

621
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:07,517
-Want me to cook something?
-Nah, just go to sleep already.

622
00:37:09,102 --> 00:37:10,103
Help yourself.

623
00:37:10,186 --> 00:37:12,230
[Beomki] Yes, thank you.
What's this? Kimchi?

624
00:37:12,313 --> 00:37:15,233
-[chuckles] Thank you, Granny. Good night.
-[Granny] Night.

625
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,694
[Beomki] I wish you a long
and healthy life.

626
00:37:17,777 --> 00:37:19,070
[fire continues crackling]

627
00:37:21,614 --> 00:37:22,907
[cell phone vibrating]

628
00:37:26,828 --> 00:37:29,289
INCOMING CALL

629
00:37:29,372 --> 00:37:31,416
[♪ foreboding music playing]

630
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:35,128
[line ringing]

631
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:41,926
[cell phone continues vibrating]

632
00:37:48,850 --> 00:37:50,143
[line continues ringing]

633
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:51,728
[line connects]

634
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:53,188
Hey.

635
00:37:54,898 --> 00:37:56,274
Where are you?

636
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:01,613
Somewhere safe. Why? Where are you?

637
00:38:02,530 --> 00:38:06,201
I just checked into a random motel.

638
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,786
Then just hole up in there.

639
00:38:07,869 --> 00:38:09,496
We're getting out of here tomorrow.

640
00:38:09,579 --> 00:38:10,580
Where are you going?

641
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:11,998
Why do you want to know?

642
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,751
Hey, take me with you.

643
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:15,919
Don't be ridiculous.

644
00:38:16,586 --> 00:38:18,338
I'm freaking out here.

645
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:20,173
Why are you acting like a moron?

646
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:22,842
Just lay low for a while,
then make your move. Got it?

647
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:25,011
Hey, Beomki!

648
00:38:28,765 --> 00:38:31,309
You bastard.
You two are the ones who killed someone.

649
00:38:31,392 --> 00:38:33,061
What are you going to do about this?

650
00:38:33,603 --> 00:38:35,396
[♪ ominous music playing]

651
00:38:38,441 --> 00:38:40,568
We're flying out of Busan
first thing tomorrow.

652
00:38:41,486 --> 00:38:42,821
I'll call you once I'm there.

653
00:38:50,245 --> 00:38:52,080
[♪ tense music playing]

654
00:39:12,475 --> 00:39:13,893
[sighs in exasperation]

655
00:39:13,977 --> 00:39:14,978
What is it?

656
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:18,940
It's just...

657
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:20,942
We don't know where they're headed,

658
00:39:21,526 --> 00:39:23,611
and catching someone
at an airport isn't easy.

659
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:25,989
They're ruthless killers,
so if we're not careful,

660
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:27,282
civilians could get hurt.

661
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:30,326
[sighs] We won't be able to stop them
at the entrance.

662
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:31,744
It'll have to be at security.

663
00:39:32,662 --> 00:39:34,789
-Notify the airport first.
-Got it.

664
00:39:34,873 --> 00:39:36,624
-I'll report to the chief.
-[Junyoung] Okay.

665
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:40,044
[Kyungjin] I got their location.

666
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:44,674
I got them as far as Wonsan-eup in Daegu,
but nothing after that.

667
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:46,885
Wonsan-eup, Daegu?

668
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:52,348
FAMILY RECORDS
JANG JAECHUN

669
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:53,933
Wonsan-eup, Daegu.

670
00:39:54,017 --> 00:39:55,727
Jang's grandma lives there.

671
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:57,437
[♪ tense music playing]

672
00:40:01,441 --> 00:40:02,650
[mouse clicks]

673
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:05,445
SATELLITE MAP SEARCH

674
00:40:08,823 --> 00:40:10,325
4-26 DURE-GIL, WONSAN-EUP, DAEGU

675
00:40:10,950 --> 00:40:12,869
That's right. I got them as far as here.

676
00:40:14,329 --> 00:40:15,914
Let's go catch them now.

677
00:40:15,997 --> 00:40:17,582
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

678
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:21,002
Let's go!

679
00:40:22,170 --> 00:40:23,171
Move out.

680
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:34,223
-It'll take 3 hours and 20 minutes.
-Huh?

681
00:40:36,976 --> 00:40:38,102
-Hold on.
-[tires screech]

682
00:40:42,982 --> 00:40:44,192
That's way too long.

683
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:47,695
These guys are smart.
What if they catch on and bolt?

684
00:40:49,197 --> 00:40:50,406
Then what else can we do?

685
00:40:52,075 --> 00:40:53,242
[sighs deeply]

686
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:55,536
[♪ upbeat music playing]

687
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:01,876
[cell phone vibrating]

688
00:41:13,805 --> 00:41:15,098
Yes, Detective Jin.

689
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,141
[Isoo] Mr. Choi, where are you?

690
00:41:17,225 --> 00:41:18,726
I'm in the helicopter.

691
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:20,353
I was in Ulsan until now.

692
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:21,729
No way.

693
00:41:21,813 --> 00:41:24,357
I need the chopper.
Bring it to the station.

694
00:41:24,440 --> 00:41:25,441
What?

695
00:41:25,525 --> 00:41:27,151
I need to catch some hitmen.

696
00:41:27,235 --> 00:41:28,695
Please be quick.

697
00:41:28,778 --> 00:41:30,655
-[line disconnects]
-[sighs in exasperation]

698
00:41:35,243 --> 00:41:36,452
Turn the chopper around.

699
00:41:37,412 --> 00:41:38,830
[helicopter whirring]

700
00:41:45,795 --> 00:41:47,213
I'll get a car here right away.

701
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:48,715
[chuckles softly]

702
00:41:49,674 --> 00:41:50,717
[sighs wearily]

703
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,260
[♪ ominous music playing]

704
00:41:59,475 --> 00:42:00,560
[Seokho] Beomki!

705
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:05,273
If we somehow get found out,

706
00:42:06,107 --> 00:42:08,693
then we kill those two
and the two of us just disappear.

707
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:11,446
If I ever call you "Beomki,"

708
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:12,739
that's the signal.

709
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:27,962
[sniffles]

710
00:42:37,638 --> 00:42:39,515
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

711
00:42:56,491 --> 00:42:57,617
There it is.

712
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,415
-Get ready.
-Yes, ma'am.

713
00:43:04,499 --> 00:43:05,541
Yes, ma'am.

714
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,543
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

715
00:43:11,714 --> 00:43:13,091
[water running]

716
00:43:20,389 --> 00:43:22,016
[♪ ominous music playing]

717
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,727
[Taegwang breathing heavily]

718
00:43:24,811 --> 00:43:26,729
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

719
00:43:47,542 --> 00:43:49,043
[continues breathing heavily]

720
00:44:03,099 --> 00:44:04,517
[Granny] Jaechun, is that you?

721
00:44:06,561 --> 00:44:08,146
[♪ ominous music playing]

722
00:44:30,001 --> 00:44:31,127
[door creaking]

723
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:33,963
[gate clangs]

724
00:44:48,436 --> 00:44:49,770
What happened here?

725
00:44:50,605 --> 00:44:52,440
[panting]

726
00:45:03,159 --> 00:45:04,493
[door creaking]

727
00:45:04,577 --> 00:45:06,287
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

728
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:08,748
[whispering] Detective Joo.

729
00:45:19,008 --> 00:45:20,009
[Kyungjin] Ma'am.

730
00:45:20,092 --> 00:45:21,761
[♪ ominous music playing]

731
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:26,474
[gasps, grunts]

732
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:27,892
[all sigh in relief]

733
00:45:31,020 --> 00:45:32,188
Who are you?

734
00:45:32,271 --> 00:45:33,814
[♪ somber music playing]

735
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:38,152
Stay with her.

736
00:45:38,236 --> 00:45:39,320
Got it.

737
00:45:41,072 --> 00:45:42,949
[door creaking, closes]

738
00:45:43,032 --> 00:45:45,826
Ma'am, we're police officers.

739
00:45:45,910 --> 00:45:46,911
What?

740
00:45:47,787 --> 00:45:51,332
Why are you here?
Did Jaechun do something bad again?

741
00:45:51,415 --> 00:45:52,458
Well...

742
00:45:56,921 --> 00:45:59,173
[Hyera] Yes, please send
the forensics team.

743
00:45:59,799 --> 00:46:01,259
They're both dead.

744
00:46:02,718 --> 00:46:05,221
[Junyoung] I need a patrol unit
and an ambulance here.

745
00:46:05,846 --> 00:46:08,641
There's also an elderly lady here,
and she's quite shaken up.

746
00:46:08,724 --> 00:46:10,559
We'll need backup.

747
00:46:10,643 --> 00:46:12,561
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

748
00:46:39,088 --> 00:46:40,381
They haven't been dead long.

749
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:43,926
-Did they kill each other?
-Why? They were planning to run.

750
00:46:48,222 --> 00:46:50,141
Did they get into a drunken fight?

751
00:46:50,224 --> 00:46:53,602
Killing the suspects
to make it the perfect crime.

752
00:46:55,980 --> 00:46:57,940
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

753
00:47:20,379 --> 00:47:22,214
There are three kinds of cigarettes.

754
00:47:26,427 --> 00:47:28,179
They haven't been dead long,

755
00:47:29,388 --> 00:47:30,556
so the perp's still here.

756
00:47:34,477 --> 00:47:36,479
Kyungjin, don't come outside.

757
00:47:36,562 --> 00:47:38,272
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

758
00:47:39,023 --> 00:47:42,485
Oh. It's all right, ma'am.
I'm sure it's nothing.

759
00:47:58,042 --> 00:47:59,126
[Taegwang exclaims]

760
00:47:59,418 --> 00:48:00,920
[blade swishing]

761
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:02,546
[both grunting]

762
00:48:06,050 --> 00:48:07,885
[Isoo grunting]

763
00:48:11,055 --> 00:48:12,139
[exclaims]

764
00:48:15,184 --> 00:48:16,852
[both grunting]

765
00:48:20,106 --> 00:48:21,524
[objects clattering]

766
00:48:27,154 --> 00:48:28,364
[gunshot]

767
00:48:31,659 --> 00:48:32,785
[panting] The next one's live.

768
00:48:34,120 --> 00:48:37,581
Want to see who's faster,
you or a bullet? Huh?

769
00:48:40,084 --> 00:48:41,210
[Isoo grunts]

770
00:48:41,293 --> 00:48:42,711
[♪ gripping music playing]

771
00:48:52,596 --> 00:48:53,722
[panting]

772
00:48:54,765 --> 00:48:56,267
Jin Isoo!

773
00:48:56,350 --> 00:48:57,351
Please.

774
00:49:06,569 --> 00:49:07,945
[Hyera panting]

775
00:49:08,654 --> 00:49:09,864
[Taegwang groaning]

776
00:49:09,947 --> 00:49:11,574
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

777
00:49:12,241 --> 00:49:14,118
-[groaning]
-Hold still!

778
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:19,790
[panting] I'm basically a sniper, right?

779
00:49:19,874 --> 00:49:21,625
You should've aimed a little higher.

780
00:49:22,251 --> 00:49:23,878
-Seriously?
-Just kidding.

781
00:49:24,462 --> 00:49:25,463
Good shot.

782
00:49:26,338 --> 00:49:27,631
I taught you well.

783
00:49:28,382 --> 00:49:30,301
That's not what's important here.

784
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:33,262
-I'm basically John Wick.
-[scoffs]

785
00:49:34,054 --> 00:49:35,181
[groans]

786
00:49:36,765 --> 00:49:38,058
Hey, are you hurt?

787
00:49:38,142 --> 00:49:39,643
It's just a scratch.

788
00:49:42,897 --> 00:49:44,690
[exclaiming in pain]

789
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:46,817
Hold still. It's to stop the bleeding.

790
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:48,736
That really hurts. [screams]

791
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:50,654
-[groans]
-[sighs softly]

792
00:49:50,738 --> 00:49:51,989
[siren blaring distantly]

793
00:49:59,622 --> 00:50:00,831
[Isoo] Oh...

794
00:50:01,415 --> 00:50:02,583
What's that?

795
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:03,667
Pain medication.

796
00:50:03,751 --> 00:50:07,004
[grunts] Don't give him that.
He needs to suffer a bit more.

797
00:50:07,087 --> 00:50:09,215
Give it to me. I'm in a lot of pain.

798
00:50:09,298 --> 00:50:10,633
[♪ quirky music playing]

799
00:50:10,716 --> 00:50:12,510
You asshole, you.

800
00:50:12,593 --> 00:50:14,053
How dare you throw chilis at me?

801
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:17,181
Guess you couldn't outrun a bullet, huh?

802
00:50:18,098 --> 00:50:19,183
[muttering] Asshole.

803
00:50:23,938 --> 00:50:25,940
We've become a real married couple.

804
00:50:26,023 --> 00:50:28,567
-That's what I think.
-[both chuckle]

805
00:50:28,651 --> 00:50:31,028
[Isoo] What a lovey-dovey couple, huh?

806
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:32,112
[in English] Nice weather.

807
00:50:32,821 --> 00:50:35,491
[in Korean] But what a shame.
It's time to say goodbye.

808
00:50:36,242 --> 00:50:38,202
Oh, you even had a baby?

809
00:50:38,285 --> 00:50:39,828
Is it a boy, or a girl?

810
00:50:40,621 --> 00:50:41,956
-[barking]
-[exclaims]

811
00:50:42,498 --> 00:50:43,707
[snarling]

812
00:50:43,791 --> 00:50:44,792
It's a puppy.

813
00:50:45,376 --> 00:50:46,544
It was a puppy.

814
00:50:46,627 --> 00:50:47,628
[Hyera] Nam Jaeguk.

815
00:50:47,711 --> 00:50:50,839
You are hereby under arrest
for soliciting the murder of Kim Minseo.

816
00:50:50,923 --> 00:50:54,218
You have the right to an attorney
and the right to remain silent.

817
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:56,345
You won't be penalized
for remaining silent.

818
00:50:56,428 --> 00:50:58,138
-Got all that?
-I was just...

819
00:50:58,222 --> 00:51:00,099
-I was taking a walk with my employee.
-Honey.

820
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:02,476
I was just...

821
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:05,396
Did you really not know
that your boyfriend killed his wife?

822
00:51:08,899 --> 00:51:10,859
You don't seem that oblivious.

823
00:51:12,111 --> 00:51:13,946
If you didn't know before, now you do.

824
00:51:15,155 --> 00:51:16,991
Someone died because of you.

825
00:51:20,035 --> 00:51:21,412
Mmm. [clicking tongue]

826
00:51:23,330 --> 00:51:24,790
[Jaeguk mutters]

827
00:51:25,791 --> 00:51:27,167
Is it a crime to take a walk...

828
00:51:28,419 --> 00:51:29,461
[exhales deeply]

829
00:51:30,379 --> 00:51:31,755
[van door slides open]

830
00:51:34,133 --> 00:51:35,301
Oh...

831
00:51:35,384 --> 00:51:37,052
You two haven't met before, right?

832
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:39,013
Say hello. This is... No, this person.

833
00:51:39,096 --> 00:51:41,682
This is the scumbag
who asked you to kill his wife.

834
00:51:41,765 --> 00:51:43,976
And this is the hitman who got the job.

835
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:47,646
You should become friends.
You'll be cellmates soon.

836
00:51:47,730 --> 00:51:49,023
Let's go.

837
00:51:49,106 --> 00:51:50,107
Yes, ma'am.

838
00:51:50,482 --> 00:51:51,984
-[engine starts]
-[siren blaring]

839
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:53,652
[♪ upbeat quirky music playing]

840
00:51:55,154 --> 00:51:56,155
[siren blaring]

841
00:51:56,238 --> 00:51:58,324
-[reporter 1] They're here!
-[reporters clamoring]

842
00:51:58,741 --> 00:51:59,908
[tires screech]

843
00:52:01,994 --> 00:52:02,995
[Isoo] Hurry up.

844
00:52:04,246 --> 00:52:05,497
Take his picture.

845
00:52:05,581 --> 00:52:06,957
Here.

846
00:52:08,125 --> 00:52:09,501
[reporters continue clamoring]

847
00:52:17,509 --> 00:52:19,720
-Good job. Thanks.
-Thank you for your hard work.

848
00:52:19,803 --> 00:52:21,847
-Hey, take them away.
-[all] Yes, sir.

849
00:52:29,146 --> 00:52:30,147
Let's go.

850
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:36,445
Heaven's on my side.

851
00:52:37,071 --> 00:52:38,906
Ah, another case closed.

852
00:52:41,742 --> 00:52:43,202
[reporters continue clamoring]

853
00:52:44,161 --> 00:52:45,371
[reporter 2] Please look this way!

854
00:52:45,996 --> 00:52:47,122
[groans softly]

855
00:52:47,915 --> 00:52:50,417
This way? Where? Like this?

856
00:52:51,001 --> 00:52:52,002
It's not over yet.

857
00:52:52,961 --> 00:52:53,962
Jin Isoo caught them.

858
00:52:54,046 --> 00:52:55,464
It was Jin Isoo.

859
00:52:57,549 --> 00:53:01,470
Now, let's walk through the case
to find out what happened.

860
00:53:01,553 --> 00:53:03,681
Mr. Nam Jaeguk here

861
00:53:03,764 --> 00:53:07,393
was suspicious of his wife and asked for
an investigation into her movements.

862
00:53:07,476 --> 00:53:09,436
-Exactly.
-And Mr. Dopey...

863
00:53:10,521 --> 00:53:14,358
Mr. Myeong Seokho here
gave the job to Mr. Yu Taegwang.

864
00:53:14,441 --> 00:53:16,527
I only made the introduction.

865
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:19,029
Sir.

866
00:53:20,364 --> 00:53:21,657
[Isoo] Then, Mr. Yu Taegwang,

867
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:24,201
you committed a murder
nobody hired you to commit.

868
00:53:25,786 --> 00:53:31,375
But how did you know
that Mr. Nam Jaeguk wanted his wife dead?

869
00:53:32,042 --> 00:53:34,837
Are you psychic? Can you read minds?

870
00:53:34,920 --> 00:53:36,463
That's exactly it.

871
00:53:36,547 --> 00:53:38,173
I never asked them to kill her.

872
00:53:38,257 --> 00:53:42,219
For God's sake,
why did you do something so stupid?

873
00:53:43,887 --> 00:53:44,972
[splutters]

874
00:53:45,055 --> 00:53:46,473
[chuckles]

875
00:53:47,725 --> 00:53:49,059
[sighs]

876
00:53:49,143 --> 00:53:50,436
You pieces of shit.

877
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:54,231
-What the hell did you just...
-I told you.

878
00:53:54,314 --> 00:53:55,899
[♪ tense music playing]

879
00:53:55,983 --> 00:53:57,818
If I go down, we all go down together.

880
00:53:59,987 --> 00:54:01,697
I recorded all the phone calls.

881
00:54:12,082 --> 00:54:13,500
[Seokho] He's called Nam Jaeguk.

882
00:54:14,126 --> 00:54:15,294
He's having an affair.

883
00:54:16,378 --> 00:54:19,173
He wants us to kill his wife
and make it look like a robbery.

884
00:54:19,882 --> 00:54:22,593
[in English] Game over, loser!

885
00:54:22,676 --> 00:54:25,345
-[in Korean] This is a fake voice.
-Get up.

886
00:54:26,180 --> 00:54:28,348
Don't be ridiculous, Mr. Dopey PI.

887
00:54:28,432 --> 00:54:30,517
[Seokho] This is AI-generated!

888
00:54:31,560 --> 00:54:34,146
Want to turn yourself in?
You'll feel better afterward.

889
00:54:35,355 --> 00:54:37,191
It's not a crime to fall in love, right?

890
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:38,692
I've been in love, too.

891
00:54:38,776 --> 00:54:41,111
It happens. We're only human.

892
00:54:43,071 --> 00:54:44,239
[door closes]

893
00:54:50,245 --> 00:54:53,457
Write down the identities
of the skeletal remains you buried.

894
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:57,377
Skeletal remains?

895
00:54:59,713 --> 00:55:01,215
I'm not sure what you mean.

896
00:55:02,049 --> 00:55:05,469
Jang Jaechun and Jo Beomki
were the ones who carried out the murders.

897
00:55:07,262 --> 00:55:09,515
But they killed each other,

898
00:55:10,724 --> 00:55:13,185
so your sentence won't be too harsh.

899
00:55:13,268 --> 00:55:15,020
You'll be better off if you cooperate.

900
00:55:15,103 --> 00:55:16,522
[♪ ominous music playing]

901
00:55:31,411 --> 00:55:32,538
[pen clicks]

902
00:55:42,130 --> 00:55:43,465
[pen scratching]

903
00:55:46,051 --> 00:55:48,595
KIM JIHUN, OH SEA, HAN MINJAE

904
00:55:58,313 --> 00:56:00,148
Let me tell you something in return.

905
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,861
That abandoned house
you used as a burial site,

906
00:56:05,654 --> 00:56:08,282
there was a robbery
and murder there 10 years ago.

907
00:56:12,869 --> 00:56:15,622
The killer's DNA was found at the scene,

908
00:56:15,706 --> 00:56:17,833
but there was no suspect
to match it against.

909
00:56:18,792 --> 00:56:21,378
Why would you have used
that place as a burial site?

910
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:26,675
Is it possible that was your first murder?

911
00:56:26,758 --> 00:56:27,968
DNA ANALYSIS REPORT

912
00:56:29,344 --> 00:56:33,599
The DNA found at the abandoned house
matched your DNA.

913
00:56:40,647 --> 00:56:42,399
Jo Beomki and Jang Jaechun.

914
00:56:43,483 --> 00:56:45,444
You killed them too, didn't you?

915
00:56:49,239 --> 00:56:51,283
And you washed the blood off
in the bathroom.

916
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:57,289
[breathing heavily]

917
00:57:00,626 --> 00:57:02,127
[Hyera] We found your fingerprint there.

918
00:57:06,882 --> 00:57:09,009
You thought you could play us, didn't you?

919
00:57:11,303 --> 00:57:12,512
The perfect crime?

920
00:57:13,805 --> 00:57:14,890
That doesn't exist.

921
00:57:23,774 --> 00:57:25,400
[doorbell rings]

922
00:57:26,318 --> 00:57:27,319
[door unlocks, beeps]

923
00:57:29,988 --> 00:57:32,783
We're sorry for everything.

924
00:57:35,535 --> 00:57:36,620
The real culprit

925
00:57:38,121 --> 00:57:39,122
has been arrested.

926
00:57:41,667 --> 00:57:43,543
[♪ poignant music playing]

927
00:57:45,128 --> 00:57:46,380
[sniffling]

928
00:57:47,923 --> 00:57:49,257
[sobbing]

929
00:57:56,056 --> 00:57:57,933
[Isoo] "The brave citizen award."

930
00:57:58,016 --> 00:58:01,061
"Park Ahin, of Myeongun Middle School,
Grade 9, Class 1."

931
00:58:01,144 --> 00:58:03,897
"In recognition
of your unwavering support of

932
00:58:03,980 --> 00:58:06,525
and cooperation with law enforcement,

933
00:58:06,608 --> 00:58:09,528
and for your assistance
in the arrest of a dangerous criminal,

934
00:58:09,611 --> 00:58:10,904
we award this commendation."

935
00:58:10,987 --> 00:58:12,906
"February 10, 2025."

936
00:58:12,989 --> 00:58:15,826
"Gwon Taegyun,
Chief of Police, Gangha Police Station."

937
00:58:16,368 --> 00:58:18,662
You're all here.

938
00:58:18,745 --> 00:58:20,956
-Congratulations, Ahin.
-Thank you.

939
00:58:21,957 --> 00:58:23,333
This is a gift from me.

940
00:58:23,417 --> 00:58:25,127
[♪ uplifting music playing]

941
00:58:25,752 --> 00:58:29,047
It's the only one in the world.
Custom-made in 24-karat gold.

942
00:58:29,131 --> 00:58:33,343
[chuckles] I'll study really hard
and become a detective like you.

943
00:58:33,427 --> 00:58:34,803
[Isoo sighs thoughtfully]

944
00:58:34,886 --> 00:58:36,096
That might be a challenge.

945
00:58:36,972 --> 00:58:39,391
The goal of a cool detective like me
might be hard to reach.

946
00:58:39,975 --> 00:58:41,476
Aim for Detective Joo here.

947
00:58:43,478 --> 00:58:45,355
Here, let's meet again as colleagues.

948
00:58:45,439 --> 00:58:46,606
Okay.

949
00:58:46,690 --> 00:58:49,609
[Taegyun] All right, back to work.
I'm off.

950
00:58:49,693 --> 00:58:50,777
-Sir.
-[Taegyun] What?

951
00:58:50,861 --> 00:58:53,071
-We've earned a vacation.
-What do you mean?

952
00:58:53,155 --> 00:58:55,323
You were just doing your duty
as detectives.

953
00:58:55,407 --> 00:58:56,992
Get your photos taken.

954
00:58:57,075 --> 00:59:00,454
We were doing our duty,
but we still busted a murder ring.

955
00:59:09,212 --> 00:59:11,423
[♪ enthralling music playing]

956
00:59:11,506 --> 00:59:13,300
[slow, echoing footsteps]

957
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:48,668
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 4

958
00:59:48,752 --> 00:59:50,170
CONCIERGE MANAGER
OH MINYEONG

959
00:59:50,253 --> 00:59:52,255
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

960
01:00:11,274 --> 01:00:14,694
Special Cast.
Lee Hakju, Park Jungpyo, Kwon Seungwoo

961
01:00:14,778 --> 01:00:18,198
Special Cast.
Park Soi

962
01:00:25,288 --> 01:00:27,207
[receptionist] Room 709
was unoccupied yesterday.

963
01:00:27,290 --> 01:00:29,459
[Hyera] That room has been vacant
for two months.

964
01:00:29,543 --> 01:00:32,254
[Isoo] Why did she go
to an unoccupied room alone?

965
01:00:32,337 --> 01:00:34,673
-Have you seen anyone suspicious lately?
-The ugly guy?

966
01:00:34,756 --> 01:00:36,341
-Chunsik?
-Isoo!

967
01:00:36,466 --> 01:00:38,301
I asked her out.

968
01:00:38,844 --> 01:00:40,804
The seventh floor camera isn't broken.

969
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:42,013
I was following the CEO's orders.

970
01:00:42,097 --> 01:00:45,851
There was an assault here last Wednesday.
He tried to drag her into Room 709?

971
01:00:46,935 --> 01:00:49,354
It did seem like
she was seeing someone lately.

972
01:00:49,437 --> 01:00:50,897
[man] I think it was one
of the hotel staff.

973
01:00:50,981 --> 01:00:52,399
[Hyera] Are you going to keep interfering?

974
01:00:52,482 --> 01:00:54,401
[Isoo] What was he doing
with the cameras off?

975
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:56,152
I found something
that looks like a bloodstain.

976
01:00:56,236 --> 01:00:58,363
Let's go.
The suspect is on the seventh floor.

977
01:00:58,446 --> 01:01:00,323
[Hyera] Watch out! Step on it.

978
01:01:00,407 --> 01:01:01,700
[exclaims]

979
01:01:05,203 --> 01:01:06,204
[man] Yes.

980
01:01:06,663 --> 01:01:08,039
I just arrived.

981
01:01:08,874 --> 01:01:09,875
Yes.

982
01:01:10,709 --> 01:01:11,751
I'll see you tomorrow.

983
01:01:11,835 --> 01:01:13,086
[♪ pensive music playing]

984
01:01:13,169 --> 01:01:14,296
[line disconnects]

985
01:01:23,263 --> 01:01:24,806
The chairman is waiting for you.

986
01:01:25,515 --> 01:01:27,893
I'll be leaving soon.
I have no business with him.

987
01:01:27,976 --> 01:01:29,394
He ordered you to come home.

988
01:01:43,199 --> 01:01:44,576
Korea...

989
01:01:45,327 --> 01:01:48,038
has too many security cameras.

990
01:01:49,456 --> 01:01:50,707
[chuckles softly]

991
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:53,627
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
